From 87af57cab4791441bdbfe0790b6ee71f48075579 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Tue, 10 Nov 2026 23:46:31 -0600
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] Compliance: allow list, fail-closed checks in scripts 1
 and 2, in-kernel guard, tests

- bench/compliance.py: block list (more organisations, substring name match) plus allow list
  (APPROVED_ORGS, REVIEWED, APPROVED_OLLAMA); the pulled tag and its GGUF repo are checked too;
  anything unreadable or too deep is refused
- scripts/build_bundle.py: uses bench/compliance.py only (no built-in copy), fails closed,
  records each model's lineage, copies the rules into the bundle
- scripts/run_benchmark.py: offline compliance check before anything runs
- bench/kaggle_hpo.py: repeats the name rules before each pull; stops if RAG-HPO leaves SapBERT
- bench/test_compliance.py: runs in the scout and benchmark workflows
- removed the retired, unfiltered pipeline/ and kaggle/ folders and three listed models from
  bench/extra_models.json

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.2 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01WcVFvpGx3PGn3MrZ4dRRSj
