index 7d1972b..0f4e53d 100644
--- a/docs/index.html
+++ b/docs/index.html
@@ -113,7 +113,7 @@ td.wrap{white-space:normal;min-width:220px;color:var(--muted)}
         <li>Every model gets the same 24 documents: 12 hand-picked ID-68 notes and 12 hand-picked GSC+ abstracts, chosen for epilepsy and neurodevelopmental findings (and, in ID-68, negated findings). With the same documents and the same scoring, every model on the page is directly comparable. A small control model is re-run each time to catch changes in the environment.</li>
         <li>Models over 15B run only when the benchmark is started with "include 15B+ models" ticked; models over 40B need the lab server.</li>
         <li>"Worth a server test" means the model beats the best selected baseline by at least 0.03 F1 on every dataset it was tested on, with no more negation errors. It is a prompt to look closer, not a decision to switch.</li>
-        <li>"Blocked" models come from a developer on the Texas prohibited technologies list, which UT System follows, or are built on such a model (fine-tunes, distills, quantized copies). They are not screened or flagged for the lab server. Earlier results for them stay visible for reference.</li>
+        <li>Models from a developer on the Texas prohibited technologies list, which UT System follows, or built on such a model (fine-tunes, distills, quantized copies), are not screened, not listed and never sent to the lab server.</li>
         <li>"Needs review" or "Not approved yet" means the model's developer is not on the lab's approved list, or the model it was built on could not be confirmed. It is not screened until a person has read its card and approved it.</li>
         <li>Scores are document-level, so they compare with document-level results in the literature (for example PhenoTagger), not mention-level ones.</li>
       </ul>
